{"id":254,"slug":"the-last-emperor","title":"The Last Emperor","year":1987,"country":"China, United Kingdom, Italy, France","duration":163,"spine":422,"url":"https://www.criterion.com/films/254-the-last-emperor","cover":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/criterion-production/films/0d98b77f2fc528a8eb2e980f290093a7/arvPvp4qN4JfMfgaOrM2c3QJ4NmX4W_large.jpg","description":"Bernardo Bertolucci’s The Last Emperor won nine Academy Awards, unexpectedly sweeping every category in which it was nominated—quite a feat for a challenging, multilayered epic directed by an Italian and starring an international cast. Yet the scope of the film was, and remains, undeniably powerful—the life of Emperor Puyi, who took the throne in 1908, at age three, before witnessing decades of cultural and political upheaval within and without the walls of the Forbidden City. Recreating Qing-dynasty China with astonishing detail and unparalleled craftsmanship by cinematographer Vittorio Storaro and production designer Ferdinando Scarfiotti, The Last Emperor is also an intimate character study of one man reconciling personal responsibility and political legacy.","boxset":0,"scraped":1,"directors":[{"name":"Bernardo Bertolucci","slug":"bernardo-bertolucci"}],"cast":[{"actor":"John Lone","role":"Puyi","slug":"john-lone"},{"actor":"Joan Chen","role":"Wan Jung","slug":"joan-chen"},{"actor":"Peter O’Toole","role":"Reginald Johnston","slug":"peter-otoole"},{"actor":"Ying Ruocheng","role":"The governor","slug":"ying-ruocheng"},{"actor":"Victor Wong","role":"Chen Pao Shen","slug":"victor-wong"},{"actor":"Dennis Dun","role":"Big Li","slug":"dennis-dun"},{"actor":"Ryuichi Sakamoto","role":"Amakasu","slug":"ryuichi-sakamoto"},{"actor":"Maggie Han","role":"Eastern Jewel","slug":"maggie-han"},{"actor":"Ric Young","role":"Interrogator","slug":"ric-young"},{"actor":"Wu Jun Mei","role":"Wen Hsiu","slug":"wu-jun-mei"},{"actor":"Cary Hiroyuki Tagawa","role":"Chang","slug":"cary-hiroyuki-tagawa"},{"actor":"Jade Go","role":"Ar Mo